[{:seon.task/name "one-content-keyed-derivation"
  :seon.task/plan "Filed by worktree session agent-view, 2026-10-23, at the owner's question: one universal cache, with easy rules for when to recompute, shared by every worker. Root's points and global-ids' measurements are folded in. It is a new mechanism, so it goes through root's gate (AGENTS §3). It must meet AGENTS §5: \"Results are reused by input digest\" and \"Content-keyed reuse is allowed for units measured as expensive; no other caches, and never one keyed by time.\"

The owner's condition (2026-10-23, through root): it must simplify the code, a net loss of src lines, measured at merge. That is this task's first proof.

Verdict of the line count (2026-10-23, src/ only, reading, nothing run): the general mechanism, as first designed, does NOT meet it.

| reuse in src today | file:lines | lines | deleted by a derivation |
|---|---|---|---|
| ../test-results file store: result-path, greens, result-file, store-greens! | proofs.clj:121-131, 142-158 | 28 | yes |
| its callers: test-plan's :dir, the greens merge, the unstored write, :seon.config.proofs/test-results-dir, allow-lists | agent.clj:371, 379, 546-550; default.edn:305; check.clj:409; program.clj:873 | ~12 | ~10 |
| fact reader stored-greens | proofs.clj:132-141 | 10 | replaced by a lookup of the same size: net 0 |
| fact writer result-tx (its digest part) | prove.clj:32-56 | 25 | ~8 |
| prove's join (slot, same?, request) | prove.clj:60-67, 103-120 | ~28 | no: a run-admission join keyed by branch@t; extending it grows it |
| fork server reach graph, base-graph | fork_server.clj:38-56, 122-126; agent.clj:321-340 | ~33 | no: an incremental update (816 MB), not a lookup |
| import-source!'s digest skip | root.clj:636-643 | ~5 | ~3 |
| the render proc's :turn-ctx, ordered's 1000 ms term | proc.clj:257-283, 330, 370; 63-72 | ~18 | ~9 |
| **total deleted** | | | **~38-45** |

The general mechanism would add a schema entry (4-6), a lookup (~10), a store function (10-12), a size bound with eviction (15-25, no precedent in src), a digest join beside prove's (10-15), the purity check (5-10) and a config key with an entry function (5-8): **~50-90 lines, a net GAIN of ~15-50.** The large repeated work it named (per-file analysis, 8-15 s a run; the base test plan per run, 7-12 s) is in test/test_runner.clj (program-db and tests-of on every run, lines 36-43 and 165-190), not in src.

**So: do not build the general mechanism.** Build its first, net-negative step:

1. Test results are facts only. Main's :seon.proof/digest facts (seon.prove/result-tx; read by seon.proofs/stored-greens) already hold every green by its reach digest, and every process reads them from the one LMDB store directly. A fact read is about 222 µs warm and 1.2 ms cold (global-ids, 2026-10-23), and an agent reads main's head without root. Delete the ../test-results file store and its callers: about -38 lines, about 0 added. It also removes self-contained's step A, which only moves that directory.
2. Delete seon.render.proc/ordered's 1000 ms term (a reuse keyed by time, which §5 forbids). Its retirement by time belongs to `order`. About -3.
3. A second derived kind is filed only when its own count is net negative too. The help page, the attempt sections built twice per later turn (seon.context/attempt-text) and a turn's remade context each need a measured miss cost and their lines first.

The rules stay as designed, for every step:
- the key is the existing reach digest (no second hasher);
- a result is a fact with a content-id identity, never a raw key, which seon.db/collect! sweeps;
- results every agent shares go on main through root's writer;
- pure work only, by the reach walk's classification;
- a size bound, never a time bound.

Sized for one worktree session."
  :seon.task/kind :work
